MJnethack@gmail.com schrieb:
> 
> I have a pet arch-lich right now, and I'm nearly ready XL-wise to go
> on the Quest.  This pet has the annoying habit of teleporting right
> next to me, so I can't lock him in a room or otherwise keep him from
> killing things I'd like kept alive.  On the other hand, I don't want
> to leave him behind to go wild, either!  Now I've noticed that even
> though aligned priests are not cold-resistant, he has not been able to
> kill the Minetown Priest.  Is my Quest leader similarly protected?

The Minetown Priest is protected by the cloak s/he's wearing - Liches'
freezing touch (the only damaging effect they'll ever use as pet[1])
is subject to the magic cancellation roll.
The quest leader does not enjoy this sort of protection, but a pet
will _never_ attack the quest friendlies of its own accord. Only
conflict can compell it to do so.

> What happens if my Quest leader gets killed, is the game un-winnable?

If the quest leader gets killed before sending you on the quest,
you're in a serious quandary. Non-wizards still have a way to finish
the quest even in that case, but that definitely requires wishing for
an artefact and may require permanent conversion to a different
alignment.

[1] if i end up with a *Lich pet, i generally abandon it as soon as
feasible and go on to genocide liches anyway. They're awesome
opponents but totally annoying and worthless pets. I am known to cheer
if my pet lich gets swallowed by a trapper.

